        "original_id": "d63ff81a-d184-53a3-ac33-d07d20172ac9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Nike, Inc., Wieden+Kennedy\n- People: Dan Wieden, David Kennedy\n- Products: Swoosh, \"Just Do It\"\n- Topics: Advertising, brand logos\n\nFacts:\n- Dan Wieden, born in 1945, is an American advertising executive who co-founded Wieden+Kennedy and coined Nike's tagline \"Just Do It.\"\n- Dan Wieden and David Kennedy were ranked number 22 on Advertising Age's list of the 100 ad people of the 20th century.\n- The Swoosh is the logo of Nike, Inc., an American athletic shoe and clothing manufacturer.\n- In many Nike-related contexts, the tagline \"Just Do It\" appears alongside the Nike logo known as the Swoosh.\n- The Swoosh has become one of the most recognizable brand logos in the world and has been valued at $26 billion alone.",
